Statement of Work (SoW–GW-A)
(Mock Contract: NASA Goddard Space Flight Center)

 Statement of Work
Contracting Organization: NASA Goddard Space Flight Center (GSFC)
Contractor: Academic Parallel Computing Laboratory (ADVCS Program)
Project Title: Automated Classification of Compact Binary Coalescence Candidates
Contract ID: GSFC-GW-EDU-24-A

1. Objective
NASA GSFC seeks an automated software pipeline capable of scanning gravitational wave strain data to identify and classify compact binary coalescence (CBC) candidate events.
The contractor shall develop a parallel analysis tool that processes time-series strain data and produces a structured classification of candidate detections.

2. Scope of Work
The contractor shall:
Process GW strain datasets conforming to the GW Input Contract
Extract discrete feature signatures using sliding window techniques
Map extracted signatures against a provided reference catalog
Aggregate detections into a hierarchical classification tree
Produce ranked Top-K candidate events

3. Required Data Structures
The contractor shall implement and utilize:
A custom hash table for feature-to-template mapping
A tree-based aggregation structure for signal classification
A heap-based priority queue for Top-K event selection
Use of standard library equivalents is prohibited where custom ADTs are specified.

4. Deliverables
gw_results.csv – hierarchical classification output
gw_topk.csv – Top-K strongest candidate events
Fully deterministic output reproducible across parallel runs

5. Success Criteria
Correct classification of synthetic CBC signals
Efficient scaling across MPI ranks
Deterministic, contract-compliant output


